@startuml scenario-player-v2x-callflow
' Research artifact (project-researcher) — Scenario Player <-> V2X ECU call flow.
' Companion to scenario-player-v2x-callflow-messages.md. Not an HLD.
' Section dividers (==) group the exchange; only section B is on the M1 critical path.

title Scenario Player and V2X ECU — call flow (M1: receive-only)

autonumber

box "Bench Node" #DDEBF7
  participant "Scenario Player\n10.99.0.10" as SP
end box

box "V2X ECU — 10.99.0.11" #E2EFDA
  participant "below seam\nadapter (R7) + modem stub (R8)" as STUB
  participant "above seam\napplication (R9)" as APP
end box

participant "ADA ECU\n10.99.0.12:47200" as ADA

== A — Bring-up: control plane, in-node — NO wire traffic, NO authentication ==

APP -> APP : read env (LISTEN_PORT, ADA_ECU_HOST/PORT, STATION_ID)
APP -> STUB : init()
STUB --> APP : ack — idle -> initialized
APP -> STUB : configure(stationId, txProfile)
STUB --> APP : ack — initialized -> configured
APP -> STUB : subscribeRx(callback)
STUB -> STUB : bind UDP 0.0.0.0:47100
STUB --> APP : ack — configured -> rx-subscribed
SP -> SP : read env + SCENARIO_CONFIG; resolve V2X_ECU_HOST/PORT

note over SP, STUB
  No handshake, no session, no credentials on this wire.
  Connectionless broadcast semantics — production Rx is
  already "read from socket" (report section 3(b)).
  ITS security (TS 103 097 signing / PKI) ships in the
  modem and is out of scope for the whole project.
end note

== B — Broadcast Rx: bench streams C's perception (R11 -> R9) — COMMITTED PATH ==

loop every 100 ms (10 Hz, from scenario config)
  SP -> SP : advance A/B/C trajectory one tick
  SP -> SP : build CPM — header + management + OVC + PerceivedObject(C)
  SP -> SP : UPER encode (shared R1 codec)
  SP ->> STUB : UDP datagram -> 10.99.0.11:47100
  STUB -> APP : onRx(bytes) via subscribed callback
  group R9 Rx pipeline
    APP -> APP : UPER decode (Vanetza r2::Cpm)
    APP -> APP : validate — mandatory fields, ranges, staleness
    APP -> APP : dedupe on (stationId, objectId, referenceTime + measurementDeltaTime)
    APP -> APP : derive object.distance = hypot(x, y)
  end
  APP ->> ADA : R2 JSON v2x_object -> 10.99.0.12:47200
end

note over APP, ADA
  This is the whole M1 V2X data path: inform the ADA ECU
  of an obstruction outside ego's line of sight.
end note

== C — Broadcast Tx (R10) — NOT IN M1, moved to the future plan ==

note over SP, ADA #FFD9D9
  Deferred by user decision 2026-07-30. The M1 V2X ECU is
  receive-only, so this wire is unidirectional.
  No ADA -> V2X path, no CPM encoder on the ECU, no Tx port.
  R7 still declares send(); nothing calls it — the seam is
  what keeps R10 a later implementation, not a redesign.
end note

== D — Fault injection: R8 in-node + bench impairment feeding the R9 corpus ==

APP -> STUB : init() / configure() / subscribeRx()
STUB --> APP : injected fault\n(init failure | configure reject | subscription drop)
APP -> APP : log defined recovery — node never crashes
SP ->> STUB : malformed / truncated / out-of-range datagram
STUB -> APP : onRx(bytes)
APP -> APP : reject + increment counter, no forward to ADA

== E — Teardown ==

SP -> SP : scenario end — stop stream
APP -> APP : age out tracks; flush JSONL evidence log (R18)

@enduml
